comments[4]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-10-22T02:08:02.092Z","harness:codex","Duplicate check: fresh request search and open/in-progress inventories plus complete3055-item strict all-status/full corpus with no omissions found no owner for mixed-type MCP array coercion. The prior CLI JSON-tag parsing item is closed with a verified string-array fix and remains intact. This distinct case was independently reproduced on the reviewed head and belongs in the same grouped PR."
  "2026-10-22T02:13:29.853Z","harness:codex","The public stdio control reproduced the reported write on the reviewed head: mixed tags persisted as strings and the sibling title changed. Both committed create/update regressions failed before the guard. The revised SDK validates merged CSV-array inputs before conversion; valid nested string arrays still replace malformed flat values, and empty arrays remain valid. All nine linked mutation/native-admission tests pass. The independent stdio probe now returns invalid_argument_value with changed=false and preserves the original title and tags. Registry audit reports zero advisories; the first static attempt correctly refused unavailable OSV evidence, without bypass or feed-success inference."
  "2026-10-22T02:46:45.192Z","harness:codex","Final local regression evidence: all 10,982 tests pass with 3 skips; exact coverage is 100/100/100/100 over 70,250 statements, 54,018 branches, 14,476 functions and 66,569 lines. The focused nine tests and ESLint pass, and public stdio refuses the mixed tags request with changed=false while retaining original item values. Both malformed create/update cases failed before the guard; valid nested replacement and empty arrays pass. The revised local static rerun correctly refuses registry transport failure (pnpm audit eventually reports fetch failed); OSV independently completes all 568 versions with no findings. No feed, timeout or threshold is bypassed. Required hosted static, coverage and security checks remain the final merge condition."
  "2026-10-22T02:46:46.051Z","harness:codex","Review triage: the initial CodeRabbit review posted one actionable mixed-array finding, now independently reproduced and fixed. Its top-level scope warning requests removing the dependency/release checkpoint and separate executable-help intake records; retain those because the user explicitly requested GitHub/security/dependency/release intake and detailed CLI evidence in the grouped delivery. Initial Sourcery and Cubic reviews are unavailable due free-plan quotas and Greptile reports an ended trial; these notices are not approvals. Request all configured reviewers again after the revised push and inspect the exact final head before merging."
